1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,040
You can install BIPs through Enterprise Edition via the installation wizard, or you can perform

2
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:12,160
an unattended installation via the command line.

3
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:17,220
When installing silently, the required input passes in a var file, which is much more efficient

4
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:19,560
when looking to install on multiple machines.

5
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:24,480
Now, the easiest way to prepare the var file is to perform a manual installation on a single

6
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:25,480
machine.

7
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:30,360
This will generate the required var file, and it will contain the required parameters.

8
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:35,000
You can then reuse this file to perform future unattended installations.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,560
Just a note, for a single deployment of BIPs through Enterprise Edition, you only need one

10
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:43,020
license per installation, and it doesn't matter how many scanning machines you want to deploy

11
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:45,240
or how many scans you wish to run.

12
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:49,480
However, if you want to deploy BIPs through Enterprise Edition into multiple environments,

13
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:52,840
you must purchase a separate license for each one.

14
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:56,460
That includes test, dev, or staging environments.

15
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:59,920
Also note that once the unattended installation is complete, you'll then need to create the

16
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:01,520
administration user.

17
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:05,000
If you want to utilize an external database, you'll also need to manually configure the

18
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,820
connectivity to the database.

19
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:13,860
Today we'll give an example of performing an unattended installation on Windows.

20
00:01:13,860 --> 00:01:18,600
As we mentioned, it's best to perform a manual installation first using the same options that you want to

21
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:21,000
utilize for your unattended installation.

22
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:26,620
This will generate the response.var file, which will be located in the install4j subdirectory

23
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:31,020
of your installation directory, the path for which is detailed here.

24
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:36,380
We do include an example var file, but I would recommend generating your own with the latest

25
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:39,340
installer version.

26
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:40,620
Here is the command itself.

27
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:43,240
We're performing an unattended installation on Windows.

28
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:48,240
So we've got our specific release, which again, we recommend the latest one if possible.

29
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:53,640
Some optional parameters to run the installer in command line mode and unattended mode.

30
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:57,240
And then we need to specify the var file itself.

31
00:01:57,240 --> 00:01:59,240
We move to our console.

32
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,860
Enter the command.

33
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:06,860
The installation will then be performed silently.

34
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:09,860
We'll speed this section up and then we can access the console.

35
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:23,480
Now that our unattended installation is complete, we can navigate to the browser, access localhost,

36
00:02:23,480 --> 00:02:25,480
and complete our setup.

37
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:32,100
Note that we can also perform an unattended installation for external scanning machines and the process

38
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:33,100
is the same.

39
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:38,040
We perform a manual installation of a scanning machine which will generate the required var

40
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:43,320
file and parameters and we utilize the same process for an unattended installation for that

41
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,320
scanning machine.

